# Component

Function declaration (not an arrow function). Props type directly above it. Destructure props in the parameter list.

```tsx
type SignInFormProps = {
  invitationToken?: string;
};

export function SignInForm({ invitationToken }: SignInFormProps) {
  return <SignInFields token={invitationToken} />;
}
```

## Client boundary

- A **client** `page.tsx` already wraps the tree: no `"use client"`.
- A **server** `layout.tsx` or `page.tsx` imports the file and it uses hooks or browser APIs: add `"use client"` at the top.
- Never put client-only files under `app/` — see [page](./page.mdc).

## UI

Use `@workspace/design-system` (`layout/`, `forms/`, `ui/`). Prefer its props (`gap`, `width`, `variant`, `size`) over custom classes. Text size comes from `Typography` variants — see [typography](./typography.mdc).

A control reused across screens goes to `packages/design-system` as a primitive with `cva` variants, like shadcn: one file per control. See `packages/design-system/src/components/ui/button.tsx`.

## One file

One component per file. `Component.Fallback`, or a small private child, may live in the same file.

```tsx
function SignInFormFallback() {
  return <Skeleton className="h-40" />;
}

SignInForm.Fallback = SignInFormFallback;
```

## Exports

Export only the component. Never re-export hooks, utils, or types (neither `export { x } from "..."` nor `export { x }` after a local import). Callers import them from `hooks/`, `utils/`, or `types/`.

## Keep it thin

Move out of the component:

- submit flow, toasts, step state → [hook](./hook.mdc)
- parsing, mapping, predicates → [util](./util.mdc)
- copy and strings → [const](./const.mdc)

## Props

Pass ids and callbacks. Never pass a fetched record down: the child reads it itself through the hook.

```tsx
export function ProjectTitle() {
  const { data } = useFindProject();
  return <Typography>{data.name}</Typography>;
}
```
